use-view-formatting-for-overdue-items.formulaOrCode:
View formatting (view dropdown > Format current view > Advanced mode)
Columns needed in the view: DueDate, Status

{
  "$schema": "https://developer.microsoft.com/json-schemas/sp/v2/row-formatting.schema.json",
  "additionalRowClass": "=if([$Status] == 'Completed' || [$Status] == 'Closed' || [$DueDate] == '', '', if([$DueDate] < @now, 'sp-field-severity--blocked', if([$DueDate] <= @now + 259200000, 'sp-field-severity--warning', '')))"
}

  259200000 = 3 days in milliseconds
  sp-field-severity--blocked  : red tint       sp-field-severity--warning : amber tint
  sp-field-severity--good     : green tint     Theme-aware classes work in light and dark themes

Column formatting for the DueDate column only (Column settings > Format this column > Advanced mode)

{
  "$schema": "https://developer.microsoft.com/json-schemas/sp/v2/column-formatting.schema.json",
  "elmType": "div",
  "attributes": {
    "class": "=if([$Status] != 'Completed' && @currentField != '' && @currentField < @now, 'sp-field-severity--blocked', '')"
  },
  "style": { "padding": "0 8px", "font-weight": "=if(@currentField < @now && [$Status] != 'Completed', '600', '400')" },
  "children": [
    {
      "elmType": "span",
      "txtContent": "=if(@currentField == '', 'No due date', toLocaleDateString(@currentField) + if(@currentField < @now && [$Status] != 'Completed', ' (' + floor((Number(@now) - Number(@currentField)) / 86400000) + ' days late)', ''))"
    }
  ]
}

No-code route
  Format current view > Conditional formatting > Manage rules
    If DueDate is before Today AND Status is not equal to Completed -> pick a colour

Pair it with a view
  "Overdue" view filter: DueDate is less than [Today] AND Status is not equal to Completed

create-a-basic-form-validation-plan.formulaOrCode:
Layer 1: Dataverse (always enforced)
  Column: Required = Business required; Maximum length; Format (Email, URL, Phone); Min and max for numbers and dates
  Business rule with scope Entity for cross-field rules, for example:
    IF Needed By < Created On THEN show error "Choose a date after today."
  Duplicate detection or an alternate key where uniqueness matters.

Layer 2: Power Pages form settings (no code)
  Design studio: select the form > Edit fields
    Make this field required | custom label | description / help text
  Portal Management app > Basic Forms > open the form > Basic Form Metadata > New (Type: Attribute)
    Is Required, Required Field Error Message
    Validation Regular Expression and Validation Error Message, for example
      UK postcode   ^[A-Za-z]{1,2}[0-9][0-9A-Za-z]?\s?[0-9][A-Za-z]{2}$
      Reference     ^REQ-[0-9]{6}$
    Range (number, date), Prepopulate from the signed-in contact, Set Value On Save
  Additional Settings: Validation Summary header text, Enable CAPTCHA, attachment limits

Layer 3: JavaScript (conditional rules; convenience only)
  Portal Management > Basic Forms > Additional Settings > Custom JavaScript

  $(document).ready(function () {
    if (typeof Page_Validators === "undefined") return;

    // Require "Other details" when Category is Other (choice value 100000003)
    var v = document.createElement("span");
    v.style.display = "none";
    v.id = "contoso_otherdetailsValidator";
    v.controltovalidate = "contoso_otherdetails";
    v.errormessage = "<a href='#contoso_otherdetails_label'>Enter details for the Other category.</a>";
    v.validationGroup = "";
    v.initialvalue = "";
    v.evaluationfunction = function () {
      var isOther = $("#contoso_category").val() === "100000003";
      return !isOther || $("#contoso_otherdetails").val().trim() !== "";
    };
    Page_Validators.push(v);

    // Show or hide the field to match
    function toggle() {
      var show = $("#contoso_category").val() === "100000003";
      $("#contoso_otherdetails").closest("td").toggle(show);
    }
    $("#contoso_category").on("change", toggle);
    toggle();
  });

  Field ids are the column logical names. Lookups add _name and _entityname inputs. Dates use a
  hidden input with the ISO value plus a visible date picker.

Plan table
  Rule                               Dataverse      Form metadata     JavaScript
  Email is required and well formed  required+format   message          -
  Phone format                       -              regular expression  -
  Needed By in the future            business rule  -                  optional early check
  Other details when Category=Other  business rule  -                  validator + show/hide
  File type and size                 -              attachment settings -

Messages
  Say what to enter, not what went wrong: "Enter a phone number with area code."
  Keep the validation summary on, and link each message to its field for keyboard users.

Test
  Empty submit, each rule broken one at a time, pasted long text, and a direct Web API POST with bad data.

create-a-portal-feedback-capture-process.formulaOrCode:
Option A: built-in feedback (table: Feedback)
  Portal Management > Web Pages > open the page > set "Enable Rating" = Yes  (per page).
  Knowledge articles also support ratings and comments.
  Quick, but limited control over fields.

Option B: your own table and form (recommended)
  Table: Page Feedback (contoso_PageFeedback)
    Was this helpful   Yes/No
    Comment            Multiline text (max 1000)
    Page URL           Text (500)
    Page title         Text (200)
    Contact            Lookup (filled when signed in)
    Status reason      New | Reviewed | Actioned | No action
    Content owner      Lookup to User (set by flow)
    Created On

  Table permission
    Access type Global, privilege Create only, web roles Anonymous Users and Authenticated Users.

  Web template "Page feedback" (include it in the page template or footer)
    <div id="pf" class="page-feedback">
      <p>Was this page helpful?</p>
      <button type="button" data-v="true">Yes</button>
      <button type="button" data-v="false">No</button>
      <textarea id="pf-comment" maxlength="1000" aria-label="Tell us more (optional)" hidden></textarea>
      <button type="button" id="pf-send" hidden>Send</button>
      <p id="pf-thanks" role="status" hidden>Thank you for your feedback.</p>
    </div>
    <script>
      (function () {
        var helpful = null, box = document.getElementById("pf");
        box.querySelectorAll("button[data-v]").forEach(function (b) {
          b.addEventListener("click", function () {
            helpful = b.dataset.v === "true";
            document.getElementById("pf-comment").hidden = false;
            document.getElementById("pf-send").hidden = false;
          });
        });
        document.getElementById("pf-send").addEventListener("click", function () {
          shell.getTokenDeferred().done(function (token) {
            fetch("/_api/contoso_pagefeedbacks", {
              method: "POST",
              headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", "__RequestVerificationToken": token },
              body: JSON.stringify({
                contoso_washelpful: helpful,
                contoso_comment: document.getElementById("pf-comment").value,
                contoso_pageurl: location.pathname,
                contoso_pagetitle: document.title
              })
            }).then(function () {
              box.querySelectorAll("button, textarea").forEach(function (e) { e.hidden = true; });
              document.getElementById("pf-thanks").hidden = false;
            });
          });
        });
      })();
    </script>
  Site settings
    Webapi/contoso_pagefeedback/enabled = true
    Webapi/contoso_pagefeedback/fields  = contoso_washelpful,contoso_comment,contoso_pageurl,contoso_pagetitle

Routing flow (Dataverse: When a row is added)
  Look up the page's owner in a "Page owners" table by URL prefix; set Content owner.
  If Was this helpful = No and Comment is not empty: post to the content team's channel.
  Weekly digest: List rows from the last 7 days, group by page, send to each owner.

Triage
  New -> Reviewed within 5 working days -> Actioned (page fixed, note what changed) or No action (with reason).
  If the visitor was signed in and asked a question, reply.

Measures
  Helpful rate per page = Yes / (Yes + No), minimum 20 responses before acting on the number.
  Pages with the most "No" comments. Time from feedback to action.

Abuse and privacy
  Rate-limit through the firewall, cap the comment length, and tell visitors not to enter personal data.
  Delete feedback older than the retention period with a bulk delete job.

create-an-adaptive-card-approval-summary.formulaOrCode:
Flow outline
  Trigger: When an item is created or modified (trigger condition: Status equals Submitted)
  Compose "Card" (JSON below)
  Post card in a chat or channel            Post as: Flow bot     Post in: Chat with Flow bot
    Recipient: @{triggerBody()?['Approver']?['Email']}
    Adaptive Card: @{outputs('Card')}
  Start and wait for an approval (Approvals) for the decision,
  or use "Post adaptive card and wait for a response" with inputs on the card itself.

Card
{
  "type": "AdaptiveCard",
  "$schema": "http://adaptivecards.io/schemas/adaptive-card.json",
  "version": "1.4",
  "body": [
    { "type": "TextBlock", "text": "Approval needed", "weight": "Bolder", "color": "Accent", "size": "Small" },
    { "type": "TextBlock", "text": "@{triggerBody()?['Title']}", "weight": "Bolder", "size": "Large", "wrap": true },
    {
      "type": "ColumnSet",
      "columns": [
        { "type": "Column", "width": "stretch", "items": [
          { "type": "TextBlock", "text": "Requested by", "isSubtle": true, "spacing": "None" },
          { "type": "TextBlock", "text": "@{triggerBody()?['Author']?['DisplayName']}", "wrap": true, "spacing": "None" } ] },
        { "type": "Column", "width": "auto", "items": [
          { "type": "TextBlock", "text": "Amount", "isSubtle": true, "horizontalAlignment": "Right", "spacing": "None" },
          { "type": "TextBlock", "text": "@{formatNumber(coalesce(triggerBody()?['Amount'], 0), 'C2', 'en-GB')}", "weight": "Bolder", "horizontalAlignment": "Right", "spacing": "None" } ] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "FactSet",
      "facts": [
        { "title": "Category",  "value": "@{triggerBody()?['Category']?['Value']}" },
        { "title": "Needed by", "value": "@{if(empty(triggerBody()?['NeededBy']), 'Not set', formatDateTime(triggerBody()?['NeededBy'], 'dd MMM yyyy'))}" },
        { "title": "Cost centre", "value": "@{coalesce(triggerBody()?['CostCentre'], 'Not set')}" },
        { "title": "Submitted", "value": "@{formatDateTime(triggerBody()?['Created'], 'dd MMM yyyy HH:mm')} UTC" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "TextBlock", "text": "Justification", "weight": "Bolder", "spacing": "Medium" },
    { "type": "TextBlock", "text": "@{replace(replace(coalesce(triggerBody()?['Justification'], 'None given'), '\', '\\'), '"', '\"')}", "wrap": true, "maxLines": 6 }
  ],
  "actions": [
    { "type": "Action.OpenUrl", "title": "Open request", "url": "@{triggerBody()?['{Link}']}" }
  ]
}

Make user text safe for JSON
  Free text can contain quotes, backslashes and line breaks that break the card. Either escape it
  as above, or build the card as an object and let the flow serialise it:
    Compose "Justification safe":  @{string(json(concat('{"t":', string(coalesce(triggerBody()?['Justification'], '')), '}')))}
  Simplest reliable method: put the text in a variable of type String and use
    @{replace(replace(replace(variables('Justification'), '\', '\\'), '"', '\"'), decodeUriComponent('%0A'), '\n')}

Layout rules
  Lead with the thing being approved, then who and how much, then supporting facts.
  Four to six facts at most. Everything else is one click away.
  Set "wrap": true on any text that can be long.
  Test in the Adaptive Cards Designer with the host app set to Microsoft Teams, light and dark themes.

Decision on the same card
  Add inputs and use "Post adaptive card and wait for a response":
    { "type": "Input.Text", "id": "comments", "label": "Comments", "isMultiline": true }
  "actions": [
    { "type": "Action.Submit", "title": "Approve", "data": { "decision": "Approve" } },
    { "type": "Action.Submit", "title": "Reject",  "data": { "decision": "Reject" } }
  ]
  Read the result: body('Post_adaptive_card_and_wait_for_a_response')?['data']?['decision']

create-a-request-escalation-screen.formulaOrCode:
// Columns used: DueDate (date), Status (choice), AssignedTo (person), StatusChangedOn (date and time),
// EscalationLevel (number, default 0), EscalatedOn (date and time), EscalatedTo (person)

// Screen.OnVisible: calculate boundaries once so the filter stays delegable
UpdateContext({
    locToday: Today(),
    locStalledBefore: DateAdd(Now(), -5, TimeUnit.Days)
});

// galEscalations.Items
With(
    { overdue: Filter(Requests, Status.Value <> "Closed" && DueDate < locToday),
      stalled: Filter(Requests, Status.Value = "Waiting for approval" && StatusChangedOn < locStalledBefore) },
    Sort(
        Switch(tabView.Selected.Value, "Overdue", overdue, "Stalled", stalled, overdue),
        DueDate, SortOrder.Ascending
    )
)

// Row labels
// lblDaysLate.Text
DateDiff(ThisItem.DueDate, locToday, TimeUnit.Days) & " days overdue"
// lblDaysLate.Color
If(DateDiff(ThisItem.DueDate, locToday, TimeUnit.Days) > 10, Color.DarkRed, RGBA(161, 98, 7, 1))
// lblLevel.Text
If(ThisItem.EscalationLevel > 0, "Escalated (level " & ThisItem.EscalationLevel & ")", "Not escalated")

// Escalate button (in the row or a side panel) > OnSelect
UpdateContext({ locSaving: true });
IfError(
    With(
        { mgr: Office365Users.ManagerV2(ThisItem.AssignedTo.Email) },
        Patch(Requests, ThisItem, {
            EscalationLevel: Coalesce(ThisItem.EscalationLevel, 0) + 1,
            EscalatedOn: Now(),
            EscalatedTo: {
                Claims: "i:0#.f|membership|" & Lower(mgr.mail),
                DisplayName: mgr.displayName,
                Email: Lower(mgr.mail)
            }
        });
        Patch('Request History', Defaults('Request History'), {
            Title: "Escalated",
            RequestId: ThisItem.ID,
            Details: "Escalated to " & mgr.displayName & " by " & User().FullName & ". " & txtEscalationNote.Value
        })
    );
    Notify("Escalated", NotificationType.Success),
    Notify("Could not escalate: " & FirstError.Message, NotificationType.Error)
);
UpdateContext({ locSaving: false })

// Reassign > OnSelect
Patch(Requests, galEscalations.Selected, {
    AssignedTo: {
        Claims: "i:0#.f|membership|" & Lower(cmbNewOwner.Selected.Mail),
        DisplayName: cmbNewOwner.Selected.DisplayName,
        Email: Lower(cmbNewOwner.Selected.Mail)
    }
})

// Header counts (use collections or CountRows on small filtered sets)
// lblOverdueCount.Text : CountRows(Filter(Requests, Status.Value <> "Closed" && DueDate < locToday)) & " overdue"
// CountRows is not delegable on SharePoint. For large lists, show "500+" when the count hits the row limit,
// or keep counts in a summary list updated by a flow.

// Who can open the screen
// App.OnStart : Set(gblIsLead, !IsBlank(LookUp('App Roles', UserEmail = Lower(User().Email) && Role = "Lead")))
// Navigation button Visible : gblIsLead

// A flow on EscalationLevel change sends the notification, so the app stays fast.

create-a-delegated-approval-screen.formulaOrCode:
// List: Approval Delegations
//   ApproverEmail (text, indexed)   DelegateEmail (text, indexed)   StartDate (date)   EndDate (date)
//   Reason (text)   IsActive (Yes/No, default Yes)

// App.OnStart or screen OnVisible: who am I covering today?
Set(gblMe, Lower(User().Email));
ClearCollect(
    colCoveringFor,
    Filter('Approval Delegations',
        DelegateEmail = gblMe && IsActive && StartDate <= Today() && EndDate >= Today())
);
// Emails whose approvals I may act on (mine plus the people I cover)
ClearCollect(colApproverEmails, { Email: gblMe });
ForAll(colCoveringFor As D, Collect(colApproverEmails, { Email: Lower(D.ApproverEmail) }));

// galApprovals.Items
// "in" against a small collection is delegable for SharePoint when the left side is a text column.
// Store the approver's email in a text column (ApproverEmail) as well as the person column.
Sort(
    Filter(Requests, Status.Value = "Waiting for approval" && ApproverEmail in colApproverEmails.Email),
    Created, SortOrder.Ascending
)

// Row badge
// lblOnBehalf.Text
If(Lower(ThisItem.ApproverEmail) <> gblMe, "On behalf of " & ThisItem.Approver.DisplayName, "")

// Approve > OnSelect
IfError(
    Patch(Requests, galApprovals.Selected, {
        Status: { Value: "Approved" },
        DecisionBy: gblMe,
        DecisionOnBehalfOf: If(Lower(galApprovals.Selected.ApproverEmail) <> gblMe, galApprovals.Selected.ApproverEmail, Blank()),
        DecisionOn: Now(),
        DecisionComments: txtComments.Value
    });
    Notify("Approved", NotificationType.Success),
    Notify("Could not save: " & FirstError.Message, NotificationType.Error)
)

// Block self-approval when covering
// btnApprove.DisplayMode
If(Lower(galApprovals.Selected.Author.Email) = gblMe, DisplayMode.Disabled, DisplayMode.Edit)

// Set up my delegation (screen "My cover")
// btnSaveDelegation.OnSelect
If(
    dpEnd.SelectedDate < dpStart.SelectedDate, Notify("End date must be after the start date.", NotificationType.Error),
    Lower(cmbDelegate.Selected.Mail) = gblMe, Notify("Choose someone other than yourself.", NotificationType.Error),
    Patch('Approval Delegations', Defaults('Approval Delegations'), {
        Title: User().FullName & " -> " & cmbDelegate.Selected.DisplayName,
        ApproverEmail: gblMe,
        DelegateEmail: Lower(cmbDelegate.Selected.Mail),
        StartDate: dpStart.SelectedDate,
        EndDate: dpEnd.SelectedDate,
        Reason: txtReason.Value
    });
    Notify("Cover saved", NotificationType.Success)
)

// My current delegations, with a cancel button
// galMyCover.Items : Filter('Approval Delegations', ApproverEmail = gblMe && IsActive && EndDate >= Today())
// Cancel           : Patch('Approval Delegations', ThisItem, { IsActive: false })

// Flow side: when a request enters "Waiting for approval", look up an active delegation for the
// approver and notify the delegate as well.

create-a-role-aware-dashboard.formulaOrCode:
// List: App Roles    UserEmail (text, indexed)   Role (choice: Requester | Approver | Admin)   IsActive (Yes/No)
// Everyone is a requester by default. Rows are needed only for extra roles.

// App.Formulas (named formulas: evaluated when first used)
nfMe        = Lower(User().Email);
nfMyRoles   = Filter('App Roles', UserEmail = nfMe && IsActive);
nfIsApprover = "Approver" in nfMyRoles.Role.Value || nfIsAdmin;
nfIsAdmin    = "Admin" in nfMyRoles.Role.Value;

// Alternative: Microsoft 365 group membership (Office 365 Groups connector)
// nfIsAdmin = !IsBlank(LookUp(Office365Groups.ListGroupMembers("<group id>").value, Lower(mail) = nfMe));

// Tiles as data, filtered by role
nfTiles = Table(
    { Key: "new",      Title: "New request",       Icon: Icon.Add,          Screen: scrNewRequest, Roles: ["Requester", "Approver", "Admin"] },
    { Key: "mine",     Title: "My requests",       Icon: Icon.DocumentWithContent, Screen: scrMyRequests, Roles: ["Requester", "Approver", "Admin"] },
    { Key: "approve",  Title: "Waiting for me",    Icon: Icon.CheckBadge,   Screen: scrApprovals,  Roles: ["Approver", "Admin"] },
    { Key: "team",     Title: "Team queue",        Icon: Icon.People,       Screen: scrTeamQueue,  Roles: ["Approver", "Admin"] },
    { Key: "admin",    Title: "Settings",          Icon: Icon.Settings,     Screen: scrAdmin,      Roles: ["Admin"] }
);

// galTiles.Items
Filter(
    nfTiles,
    "Requester" in Roles.Value
        || (nfIsApprover && "Approver" in Roles.Value)
        || (nfIsAdmin && "Admin" in Roles.Value)
)
// Tile OnSelect : Navigate(ThisItem.Screen)

// Counts on tiles (load once, in parallel)
// scrHome.OnVisible
Concurrent(
    Set(gblMyOpen,    CountRows(Filter(Requests, Author.Email = nfMe && Status.Value <> "Closed"))),
    If(nfIsApprover, Set(gblWaiting, CountRows(Filter(Requests, ApproverEmail = nfMe && Status.Value = "Waiting for approval")))),
    If(nfIsApprover, Set(gblOverdue, CountRows(Filter(Requests, Status.Value <> "Closed" && DueDate < Today()))))
);
// lblCount.Text (inside the tile)
Switch(ThisItem.Key, "mine", gblMyOpen, "approve", gblWaiting, "team", gblOverdue, Blank())
// lblCount.Visible : !IsBlank(Self.Text)

// Sections that only some roles see
// conApproverSummary.Visible : nfIsApprover
// conAdminLinks.Visible      : nfIsAdmin

// Guard screens too, not just the tiles
// scrAdmin.OnVisible : If(!nfIsAdmin, Navigate(scrHome))

// Greeting
// lblHello.Text : "Hello " & First(Split(User().FullName, " ")).Value

// Security note
// Hiding a tile does not secure the data. Set list permissions or Dataverse roles so that a user
// who is not an approver cannot edit decision fields even outside the app.

create-a-reusable-command-bar.formulaOrCode:
// Component: cmpCommandBar   (Components > New component)   Height 48, Width Parent.Width
// Turn on "Access app scope" only if the component needs global variables. It does not need them.

// Custom properties
//   Commands        Input   Table     the buttons to show
//   IsBusy          Input   Boolean   disables everything while saving
//   OnCommand       Event   (behaviour property) with one parameter:  Key (Text)
//   SelectedKey     Output  Text      last pressed key

// Default value of the Commands property defines its schema
Table(
    { Key: "new",     Label: "New",     Icon: Icon.Add,    Enabled: true, Visible: true, Primary: true },
    { Key: "refresh", Label: "Refresh", Icon: Icon.Reload, Enabled: true, Visible: true, Primary: false }
)

// Inside the component: a horizontal gallery
// galCommands.Items
Filter(cmpCommandBar.Commands, Visible)
// galCommands.TemplateSize : 120      galCommands.TemplatePadding : 4

// Inside the row: a classic button (or modern button) filling the template
// btnCommand.Text         : ThisItem.Label
// btnCommand.DisplayMode  : If(cmpCommandBar.IsBusy || !ThisItem.Enabled, DisplayMode.Disabled, DisplayMode.Edit)
// btnCommand.Fill         : If(ThisItem.Primary, RGBA(0, 120, 212, 1), RGBA(0, 0, 0, 0))
// btnCommand.Color        : If(ThisItem.Primary, Color.White, RGBA(32, 31, 30, 1))
// btnCommand.AccessibleLabel : ThisItem.Label
// btnCommand.OnSelect
Set(varLastCommandKey, ThisItem.Key);      // component-scoped variable
cmpCommandBar.OnCommand(ThisItem.Key)

// SelectedKey (output) : varLastCommandKey

// ---- Using it on a screen ----
// cmpCommandBar_1.Commands
Table(
    { Key: "new",    Label: "New",    Icon: Icon.Add,   Enabled: true,                          Visible: true,      Primary: true },
    { Key: "edit",   Label: "Edit",   Icon: Icon.Edit,  Enabled: !IsBlank(galRequests.Selected), Visible: true,      Primary: false },
    { Key: "delete", Label: "Delete", Icon: Icon.Trash, Enabled: !IsBlank(galRequests.Selected), Visible: nfIsAdmin, Primary: false },
    { Key: "export", Label: "Export", Icon: Icon.Download, Enabled: true,                       Visible: nfIsApprover, Primary: false }
)
// cmpCommandBar_1.IsBusy : locSaving

// cmpCommandBar_1.OnCommand     (Key is the event parameter)
Switch(
    Key,
    "new",    NewForm(frmRequest); Navigate(scrRequestForm),
    "edit",   EditForm(frmRequest); Navigate(scrRequestForm),
    "delete", UpdateContext({ locShowConfirmDelete: true }),
    "export", ExportRequests.Run(JSON(colSelected, JSONFormat.IgnoreBinaryData))
)

// Narrow screens: show icons only
// btnCommand.Text       : If(cmpCommandBar.Width < 600, "", ThisItem.Label)
// galCommands.TemplateSize : If(cmpCommandBar.Width < 600, 48, 120)

// Share across apps
// Build the component in a component library (Apps > Component libraries), publish it, and import it into
// each app. Apps are offered the update when the library is republished.

create-a-release-notes-panel.formulaOrCode:
// List: App Release Notes
//   Title (version, for example 2.4)   ReleaseDate (date)   Summary (text)   Changes (multiple lines, plain text,
//   one change per line)   AppName (text)   IsPublished (Yes/No)
// List: App Release Views (who has seen which version)
//   Title (version)   UserEmail (text, indexed)   AppName (text)   SeenOn (date and time)

// App.Formulas
nfAppName       = "Request Hub";
nfLatestRelease = First(
    Sort(Filter('App Release Notes', AppName = nfAppName && IsPublished), ReleaseDate, SortOrder.Descending)
);

// Home screen OnVisible: show once per user per version
If(
    !IsBlank(nfLatestRelease.Title) &&
    IsBlank(LookUp('App Release Views',
        UserEmail = Lower(User().Email) && AppName = nfAppName && Title = nfLatestRelease.Title)),
    UpdateContext({ locShowReleaseNotes: true })
)

// Panel: a container over the screen
// conReleaseNotes.Visible : locShowReleaseNotes
// lblReleaseTitle.Text    : "What's new in version " & nfLatestRelease.Title
// lblReleaseDate.Text     : Text(nfLatestRelease.ReleaseDate, "d mmmm yyyy")
// lblSummary.Text         : nfLatestRelease.Summary

// galChanges.Items : one row per line of the Changes field
Filter(Split(nfLatestRelease.Changes, Char(10)), !IsBlank(Trim(Value)))
// lblChange.Text   : "•  " & Trim(ThisItem.Value)

// btnGotIt.OnSelect : record that this user has seen it
UpdateContext({ locShowReleaseNotes: false });
IfError(
    Patch('App Release Views', Defaults('App Release Views'), {
        Title: nfLatestRelease.Title,
        UserEmail: Lower(User().Email),
        AppName: nfAppName,
        SeenOn: Now()
    }),
    Blank()     // not being able to record the view should never block the user
)

// Reopen from the menu or footer
// lnkWhatsNew.OnSelect : UpdateContext({ locShowReleaseNotes: true })
// lblVersion.Text      : "Version " & nfLatestRelease.Title

// Earlier versions (optional second tab in the panel)
// galHistory.Items : Sort(Filter('App Release Notes', AppName = nfAppName && IsPublished), ReleaseDate, SortOrder.Descending)

// Lighter option without the views list: remember on the device
// OnVisible : LoadData(colSeenRelease, "seenRelease", true);
//             If(First(colSeenRelease).Version <> nfLatestRelease.Title, UpdateContext({ locShowReleaseNotes: true }))
// Got it    : ClearCollect(colSeenRelease, { Version: nfLatestRelease.Title }); SaveData(colSeenRelease, "seenRelease")
// SaveData works in the mobile player and, with limits, in browsers. The list approach works everywhere
// and tells you who has read the notes.

// Writing the notes
// Lead with what the user can now do. One line per change. No ticket numbers.
// Good:  You can now attach photos from your phone camera.
// Poor:  Implemented attachment control enhancement (CR-1182).
